      "writtenOn": "2015-03-23T12:05:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not a problem to add but as specified by Marek the primary_key\u003dTrue implies the uniqueness of the field. Previously it was there because the primary_key\u003dTrue was in both the remote_id and the idp_id and this translate to sql as PRIMARY KEY (`idp_id`.`remote_id`), this does not imply the uniqueness of the remote_id but that of the combination.\n\nThus, add only the unique id concept in remote_id does not make sense if we do not put back the idea of a primary key as a couple or some other changes.\n\nI would leave as it is now but if you (and others) prefer the unique approach for me is OK",
